# installer/linux/ ships shell scripts (some with no .sh extension -- the Debian maintainer
# scripts) and templates that run or get rendered inside a Linux container/VM. Git on this
# repository's development machine (Windows) defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout; a
# CRLF shebang line (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) fails with "bad interpreter", and a CRLF inside a
# systemd unit or logrotate config produced by sed can be just as silently wrong. Force LF here
# regardless of the checking-out machine's `core.autocrlf`, the same way the ASCII-only rule in
# doc 14 §8.4 exists for the Windows scripts' own encoding trap.
installer/linux/** text eol=lf
